34. What do miners do with the first transaction when preparing a block?
a) They use it to pay the highest-fee transaction first, so it is always the largest payment in the block
b) They leave it empty as a placeholder that is filled in once the block is mined
c) They use it to store the block’s timestamp and the nonce of the proof-of-work
d) It is a coinbase transaction specifying the recipient of the block reward
correct: d)
explanation:
The first transaction in every block is the coinbase transaction. It has no real TxIn 
(it references no previous output) and creates new coins. Its TxOut pays the block reward, plus 
the collected transaction fees, to an address chosen by the miner.

